          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP424 Edmonton Hardisty

Out with the kids to find a few caps on this beautiful day.TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684648336">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP424 Edmonton - Hardisty&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another quick find near the line between landscaped and manicured, and wild and natural.  We noticed the piece of a nearby fallen birch tree that WillowZilla had left lined up with the cap and added a piece of flagging low on a spruce tree that will hopefully remain in place longer.  TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684124433">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP424 Edmonton - Hardisty&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another quick one thanks to the context pics.  I studied them before getting here and WillowZilla's pic still held true.  A quick find thanks to that one and I was on my way.  Gorgeous day to be out and about capping.  Everything's turning green!  Really enjoying these for my week's streaking finds this week too.  :) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBC OFTH and for the quick approval, as always.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682021632">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP424 Edmonton - Hardisty&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At today's CITO event WillowZilla let me know he had just found this cap and had left it nicely exposed and a marker. Made sure to find it today to avenge our previous DNF. 

The find was so easy it made me somewhat embarrassed that we didn't find it previously. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681706802">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.556750" lon="-113.431483" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-28T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP424 - Edmonton- Hardisty&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I grew up in this area, so it's nice to return and pick up some of these markers in places i've seen before.  This was a tough one, our only tool was a screwdriver and the recent MKPerry DNF was discouraging.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The usual 'check out Coolcat21's context shot' philosophy wasn't helping much, but probably helped just enough.  We searched for 10-15 minutes before I spotted a super subtle divot hidden by cut grass that the screwdriver made the mighty ping upon stabbing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I set up a piece of local birch pointing at it and left it nicely exposed.  Extremely well preserved cap here :)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
